---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const schema={
  "@context":"https://schema.org",
  "@type":"WebPage",
  "name":"Camvella Security",
  "url":"https://camvella.com/security/",
  "about":{"@type":"SoftwareApplication","name":"Camvella","applicationCategory":"BusinessApplication"}
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Security — Camvella HOA Management Software"
  description="How Camvella approaches tenant isolation, row-level security, private document storage, role-based access, auditability and secure infrastructure."
  canonical="https://camvella.com/security/"
  schema={schema}
>
<section class="security-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section__label">Security & Trust</p>
    <h1>Protect each association.<br/>Protect each management company.</h1>
    <p>Camvella is designed around database-enforced tenant boundaries, private document storage, role-based access and audit-oriented workflows. We describe controls we can actually verify and do not advertise certifications we have not independently earned.</p>
    <div class="security-actions"><a href="/demo" class="btn btn--primary btn--lg">Book a security walkthrough</a><a href="/privacy" class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg">Privacy policy</a></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section__label">Core controls</p>
    <h2 class="section__headline">Security built into the operating model.</h2>
    <div class="security-grid">
      <article><h3>Database-enforced tenant isolation</h3><p>Camvella uses PostgreSQL Row Level Security so authenticated access is scoped to the correct management company and association context at the database layer.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Private document storage</h3><p>Association, vendor, board, resident and operational files use private storage patterns with controlled access instead of permanent public file URLs.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Role-based access</h3><p>Permissions are designed around owners, administrators, managers, accountants, board members, residents and other operational roles rather than one universal staff account.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Auditability</h3><p>Camvella includes audit-oriented records for sensitive workflows and administrative changes so authorized users can review important activity over time.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Server-side privileged access</h3><p>Service-role credentials and provider secrets are kept out of normal browser-managed settings. Privileged operations are separated from ordinary end-user access.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Encrypted transport</h3><p>Camvella is served over HTTPS and application traffic is protected in transit using modern TLS through its hosting and platform providers.</p></article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--alt">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="section__label">Buyer checklist</p>
    <h2 class="section__headline">Questions an HOA management company should ask any software vendor.</h2>
    <div class="security-checklist">
      <div><strong>Can another management company query our associations?</strong><span>Tenant boundaries should be enforced at the database layer, not only hidden in the UI.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Are documents public?</strong><span>Board, resident, vendor and financial files should use private storage and controlled access.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Who can change financial or permission settings?</strong><span>Administrative actions should be restricted to appropriate roles and reviewable where the workflow supports it.</span></div>
      <div><strong>What is independently certified?</strong><span>Camvella does not advertise SOC 2, ISO 27001 or other certifications unless independently verified.</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--dark">
  <div class="container" style="text-align:center">
    <h2 class="section__headline" style="color:#fff">Bring your security questions to the demo.</h2>
    <p class="section__subhead" style="margin:0 auto 28px;text-align:center">We would rather show the control and explain the boundary than make a broad security claim.</p>
    <a href="/demo" class="btn btn--primary btn--lg">Book a Demo</a>
  </div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.security-hero{padding:128px 0 82px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--clr-navy),#0f5965);color:#fff}
.security-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4.5rem);line-height:1.02;letter-spacing:-.04em;max-width:13ch;margin:10px 0 20px}
.security-hero p:not(.section__label){max-width:68ch;color:rgba(255,255,255,.75);font-size:1.08rem;line-height:1.7}
.security-actions{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:28px}.security-hero .btn--ghost{color:#fff;border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.25)}
.security-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:16px;margin-top:32px}
.security-grid article{padding:24px;border:1px solid var(--clr-border);border-radius:16px;background:#fff}.security-grid h3{color:var(--clr-navy);margin-bottom:9px;font-size:1rem}.security-grid p{color:var(--clr-text-soft);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.65}
.security-checklist{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:14px;margin-top:30px}.security-checklist div{padding:22px;border:1px solid var(--clr-border);border-radius:14px;background:#fff}.security-checklist strong{display:block;color:var(--clr-navy);margin-bottom:8px}.security-checklist span{color:var(--clr-text-soft);font-size:.92rem;line-height:1.6}
@media(max-width:900px){.security-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}@media(max-width:650px){.security-grid,.security-checklist{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>